    "iEM3555",
    "iEM3565",
    "iEM3455C1",
    "iEM3455C2"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "se.com",
  "description": "Three-phase DIN rail energy meters for LVCT (iEM3455/3465) or Rogowski coils (iEM3555/3565): currents, voltages, power, power factor, frequency, energies, demand, tariffs, overload alarm and setup",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-14",
  "source": "Schneider Electric, iEM3400 / iEM3500 series user manual, 7EN02-0438-15 (05/2026), Modbus register list",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "iEM3400 / iEM3500 series – User manual",
      "version": "7EN02-0438-15 (05/2026)",
      "url": "https://www.se.com/ww/en/download/document/7EN02-0438/",
      "note": "chapter Communications using Modbus: register list, data types and command interface"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU over RS485 on the iEM3455 and iEM3555; the iEM3465 and iEM3565 use BACnet MS/TP instead.",
    "Addresses are the manual's register numbers (address on the wire = register - 1).",
    "Function 03 reads; function 16 writes the tariff and sends commands. Settings marked WC in the manual are changed through the command interface (registers 5250 on), so they are listed here as read-only.",
    "Energies are given both as 64-bit integers (Wh, varh) and as 32-bit floats (kWh, kvarh).",
    "DATETIME values (4 registers) are shown as 64-bit raw values; the bit layout is in the description of register 132.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 1,
  "x_status": "official",
